---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Icons reGospeled — a gospel that heals">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">More informed &amp; dignified theology and psychology</p>
      <h1>Rediscover a gospel that heals.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Many of us were handed a God who keeps score. Icons reGospeled helps the wounded and the curious rediscover a gospel that heals — through honest theology, psychology, and real community.</p>
      <div class="cta-row center">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/reading-finder/">Find your book →</a>
        <a class="textlink" href="/course/">or take the course</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <p class="eyebrow">If this is you</p>
      <h2>You love Christ, but the loudest version of faith started to feel like a threat.</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">You went looking for something both theologically serious <em>and</em> non-shaming, and couldn't find it. Underneath is the exhaustion, the disillusionment, and the quiet fear that maybe the problem is you.</p>
      <p>It isn't. Fear-based, shame-based religion has always struggled to tell the truth about a God who is, first and last, love. The gospel was supposed to be good news — a Physician, not a scorekeeper.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- before/after gospel contrast (drag to compare) -->
  <section data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <p class="eyebrow">The same word, two very different Gods</p>
      <h2>Which gospel were you handed?</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="ba">
        <div class="ba-after"><div class="ba-inner">
          <div class="ba-col ba-scripture">
            <span class="ba-tag">Closer to the Greek &amp; Hebrew</span>
            <div class="ba-verses">
              <div class="v"><b>John 12:32</b><span>“I will <em>drag</em> all people to myself.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Galatians 2:16</b><span>Freed by the <em>faith of</em> Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 6:5</b><span>Grown together as <em>one</em> with Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Isaiah 53:10 · LXX</b><span>The Lord willed to <em>cleanse</em> him.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 3:25</b><span>The <em>mercy seat</em> — where God meets us.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ba-col ba-summary ba-summary-right">
            <span class="ba-tag">The gospel that heals</span>
            <ul><li>A Father, running toward you</li><li>A Physician, not a courtroom</li><li>Healing of the whole person</li><li>Love, first and last</li><li>You — a living icon, restored</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="ba-before"><div class="ba-inner">
          <div class="ba-col ba-summary">
            <span class="ba-tag">The God you were handed</span>
            <ul><li>A scorekeeper, arms crossed</li><li>A courtroom, always in session</li><li>Fear as the engine</li><li>Wrath, first and last</li><li>You — a problem to manage</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="ba-col ba-scripture">
            <span class="ba-tag">As it was handed</span>
            <div class="ba-verses">
              <div class="v"><b>John 12:32</b><span>“I will <em>draw</em> all people to myself.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Galatians 2:16</b><span>Freed by your <em>faith in</em> Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 6:5</b><span>Planted together with him in death.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Isaiah 53:10</b><span>“It pleased the Lord to <em>crush</em> him.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 3:25</b><span>A <em>propitiation</em> — appeasing wrath.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div></div>
        <input type="range" class="ba-range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Slide to reveal the Scriptures behind each gospel">
        <div class="ba-divider"><span class="ba-knob" aria-hidden="true">⟺</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="ba-hint">Drag either way to reveal the Scriptures behind each →</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">You're not crazy for wanting more</p>
        <h2>We've been the wounded and disillusioned too.</h2>
        <p>Icons reGospeled sits at the intersection of ancient theology, modern psychology, and relational presence. We read the Church Fathers and take the brain and the body seriously, because healing is a whole-person thing.</p>
        <p>There's a podcast, a course, a table you can actually pull up a chair to, and a curated library of the best restoration theology we know.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><span class="k">Rooted in</span><h3>The Fathers</h3><p>Irenaeus, Athanasius, the Gregorys — theosis, Christus Victor, and the restoration of the image.</p></li>
        <li><span class="k">Honest about</span><h3>The Whole Person</h3><p>Psychology in service of healing — not to replace faith, but to help it land in the body.</p></li>
        <li><span class="k">Practiced at</span><h3>The Table</h3><p>Real gatherings where you can think out loud, tell the truth, and be welcomed.</p></li>
        <li><span class="k">Building</span><h3>A Library</h3><p>A curated path through grace, hell reframed, the Fathers, psychology, and contemplation.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fathers" data-reveal aria-label="Church Fathers we read with">
    <p class="label">We read with the ancients</p>
    <div class="fathers-track">
      <span>Irenaeus of Lyons</span><span>Athanasius</span><span>Basil the Great</span><span>Gregory of Nyssa</span><span>Gregory Nazianzen</span><span>Maximus the Confessor</span><span>John Chrysostom</span><span>Origen</span><span>Irenaeus of Lyons</span><span>Athanasius</span><span>Basil the Great</span><span>Gregory of Nyssa</span><span>Gregory Nazianzen</span><span>Maximus the Confessor</span><span>John Chrysostom</span><span>Origen</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="text-align:center;">A clear path forward</p>
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">Four steps back to a gospel that heals</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <ol class="path" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <li><span class="n">1</span><div><h3>Find your next book</h3><p>Answer three questions in the Book Finder and start reading where you actually are.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">2</span><div><h3>Join the conversation</h3><p>The podcast and the Substack — deeper, freer, more honest than you were taught to expect.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">3</span><div><h3>Come to the table</h3><p>Wings, Whiskey &amp; the Word and our other gatherings. Belong before you believe it all.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">4</span><div><h3>Go deeper</h3><p>The course, <em>The Gospel You Were Never Told</em> — the good news, all the way down.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="lead" style="text-align:center;max-width:60ch;margin:32px auto 0;">Our promise: we won't shame you, rush you, or hand you slogans. We'll meet you with depth, honesty, and welcome.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="divine" data-reveal>
    <svg class="trinity" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.4"><circle cx="100" cy="72" r="46"/><circle cx="76" cy="118" r="46"/><circle cx="124" cy="118" r="46"/></g></svg>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <p class="eyebrow">What's at stake</p>
      <h2>You can stop managing your fear and start becoming a living icon again.</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <p class="lead">The alternative is staying trapped in a faith that slowly crushes you — or walking away from Christ entirely because the only version you knew was toxic. There's another road: hearing the gospel as truly good news, the healing of the whole person, and a community that thinks deeply and loves well.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="text-align:center;">Everything in one place</p>
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">Where to begin</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:36px;">
        <a class="card" href="/reading-finder/"><div class="tag">Free · start here</div><h3>The Book Finder</h3><p>Three questions, two books chosen for where you are, and a curated library of 60+ more.</p><span class="go">Find your book →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/podcast/"><div class="tag">Podcast</div><h3>Less Heresy Than Expected</h3><p>Warm, witty, theologically serious conversation for believers, doubters, and the disillusioned.</p><span class="go">Listen →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/course/"><div class="tag">Course · $20</div><h3>The Gospel You Were Never Told</h3><p>What if the Good News is actually better than you were told? Five sessions to find out.</p><span class="go">Take the course →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/community/"><div class="tag">Community</div><h3>Come to the table</h3><p>Wings, Whiskey &amp; the Word, Movies for Humans, retreats, and more.</p><span class="go">See gatherings →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="https://strengthenedbygrace.substack.com/"><div class="tag">Substack</div><h3>Strengthened by Grace</h3><p>Theological reflection, gospel interpretation, and spiritual restoration — free to read.</p><span class="go">Subscribe →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/give/"><div class="tag">Support</div><h3>Give</h3><p>Help keep the table set and the library growing. Every gift furthers the work.</p><span class="go">Give →</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow">
      <h2>Come to the table.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Start with the book most likely to meet you where you are — free, and yours in about a minute.</p>
      <div class="cta-row center" style="margin-top:24px;">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/reading-finder/">Find your book →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/community/">Find a gathering</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
